+
+## Task Control
+
+| Contract state | Execution route | State rationale |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| READY | DIRECT | Source, structural, semantic, and post-draft review gates pass; the bounded task can proceed directly to implementation. |
+
+## Objective
+
+Add an explicit JSON output option to the report command so automation can consume the same report records currently shown to terminal users.
+
+## Context / Constraints
+
+- Preserve the current human-readable output when the new option is absent.
+- Use the report command's existing record selection and ordering.
+- Do not add a new transport or persistent storage format.
+
+## Source Authority
+
+| Source | Authority | Status | Task implication |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Approved report automation request | Product outcome authority | Confirmed | Automation requires structured output without changing the existing interactive command. |
+| Current report command and focused tests | Behavior and regression baseline | Inspected | Reuse current record selection and preserve default output. |
+
+## Task Scope
+
+| Scope item | Classification | Approval impact | Notes |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| JSON output option and serializer | In scope | blocking | Emit the selected report records as valid JSON. |
+| Default terminal output regression | In scope | blocking | Existing behavior must remain unchanged without the option. |
+| Additional export formats | Out of scope | non-blocking | CSV and XML require separate outcome authority. |
+
+## Materially Verifiable Success Criteria
+
+| ID | Criterion | Proof | Required before done |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| TD-SC-1 | Invoking the report command with the JSON option exits zero and emits a parseable JSON array containing the same ordered records as the existing report selection. | Run the focused CLI fixture, parse stdout as JSON, and compare record identities and order with the fixture's expected selection. | Yes |
+| TD-SC-2 | Invoking the report command without the JSON option preserves its current stdout and exit behavior. | Run the existing report command regression test unchanged and compare its captured output with the baseline fixture. | Yes |
+
+## Incremental Value Delivery
+
+| Slice | Value proven | Risk retired | Evidence | Stop / continue decision |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Structured report output | Automation can consume the current report selection while interactive output remains stable. | Retires divergent selection logic and default-output regression risk. | Focused JSON fixture plus the existing report regression test. | Stop when both criteria pass over the same record fixture. |
+
+## Review Boundary
+
+| Boundary | In scope for review | Out of scope / follow-up | Approval impact |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Output behavior | JSON validity, record parity, ordering, and unchanged default output | Additional formats | blocking for in-scope regressions; otherwise non-blocking |
+
+## Validation / Evidence
+
+| Criterion ID | Check | Evidence | Runner / owner | Required before done |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| TD-SC-1 | Run the focused JSON CLI fixture and parse stdout. | Zero exit, parseable JSON, and exact ordered record parity. | Implementer | Yes |
+| TD-SC-2 | Run the existing default-output regression test. | Zero exit with unchanged stdout and exit behavior. | Implementer | Yes |
+
+## Execution Notes
+
+- Use the existing report selection boundary and add serialization after selection.
+- Stop if structured output requires changing record selection or default output semantics.
+
+## Follow-up / Non-blocking Work
+
+None.
